      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Mathematical data are presented supporting a relationship between road accident deaths (RAD), male and female, and ischaemic heart disease (IHD) deaths, male and female, in Australia. It is suggested that RAD on a national scale are a function of vehicle usage, for both males and females, and in turn, vehicle usage creates stress on bodily function resulting in IHD."},
